WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.050
On batarei ya sowaka.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.310
On batarei ya sowaka.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.650
On batarei ya sowaka.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.990
Katsuhiko!

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.820
He wishes...

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.390
he wishes you'd stop crying.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.490
He misses your smile.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.640
Mr. Nagumo!

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.880
A job?

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.590
It's at the MCC Corporate office.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.930
The “Tokyo Palace.”

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:04.190
It's on the waterfront.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.200
Watch out! You're going
to bump into something!

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.800
Excuse me!
Please excuse me!

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.110
I told you so!

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:31.820
Hello.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.480
Good timing. I just finished
my morning examinations.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:36.990
Seishiro!

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.290
Good morning.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.530
We bought lunch.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:47.360
I got you a fish burger
and a teriyaki sandwich.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.410
And you probably bought yourself
the usual four burgers.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.910
Life is blissful,
until it's time to diet!

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.680
Subaru, come on,
or I'll eat yours too!

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:04.390
Yes sir, I know the way. I have
a map right here, Mr. Mimura.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.260
You're the president?
Three o'clock? No, that will be fine.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.950
The MCC Corporation?

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.590
I saw them on TV.
They're over in the bay area.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.360
It looks like they're
working on something big.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.630
Yeah, it's called “Project 5.”

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:26.040
They have five “smart” buildings
wired together with fiber optics.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.910
And now they have
some work for you?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:34.880
My name is Sumeragi.
No, Su-me-ra-gi.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.050
Subaru, why are you
so damn polite?

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:42.720
You're bowing on the phone!
You look like a salaryman!

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:48.560
No, it's nothing. Right.
Thank you very much.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.540
Don't you understand
how important you are?

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.810
You're the head of
the Sumeragi family!

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.350
For over 2000 years...

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:08.910
our family has been
protecting japan spiritually!

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:13.580
I know the family isn't
very big anymore...

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:19.130
but we've always been the
greatest mediums in japan...

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:23.670
sewing the Emperor
since the tenth century!

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:29.840
You're the head of our family!
Don't be such a pathetic wimp!

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:37.170
But I'm just an ordinary medium.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:40.810
There's no such thing
as an “ordinary” medium!

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.350
So, do you have another job?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:48.950
MCC's construction crew has
had some strange accidents.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.290
Work is falling seriously behind.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:54.420
Is something
supernatural causing it?

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:56.000
I don't know.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:06:00.600
But the workers are scared.
They're afraid to work there.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.470
Is that all?

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.540
No, there's something else too.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:09.840
The president's going to
fill me in this afternoon.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.950
Zone 15 is way behind, but
we moved on to units 7 and 13.

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:25.330
So the total delay is reduced
to 96 hours of production.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.530
Even if we allow for the
effects of bad weather...

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.340
Nagumo...

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:41.850
last week's report said
efficiency was down by 5%.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.110
I've solved it.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.150
Some of the men thought
the project was cursed.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.880
I've replaced all of them.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:53.380
Your decisions have
always been a bit abrupt.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.930
We can't afford any further
delays on this project.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:03.400
This will require even harder work
from all of us at the top.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:07.730
Why are you hiring a medium?

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:09.370
Mr. President...

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.500
It's time for your medication.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:25.090
Even the government sometimes
uses the Sumeragi family.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:29.750
Often one has to do surprising
things to placate employees.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.790
Nagumo.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.980
I'll join you.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.320
You usually aren't so outgoing.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:03.590
I don't mean to intrude, but
you seem worried about the delays.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:05.820
How's your health?

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.760
Don't worry.

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:14.600
Every executive has to live
with a few chronic illnesses.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:22.280
You can't let minor obstacles
stop you if you want promotions.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:25.210
I'll keep that in mind.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.980
What's wrong?
Is it a breakdown?

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:26.300
The elevator fell?

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.750
This building really IS cursed!

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.870
What? That's terrible!

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:06.480
I promised to meet
President Mimura today.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:10.780
Too bad. Your appointment's
been canceled.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:12.620
President Mimura's over there.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.430
This is quite a surprise.

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:27.440
I hardly expected a
witch doctor to be so young.

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:29.940
I'm a medium.

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:36.950
Mr. Nagumo, about the
accidents you've been having-

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:39.210
We don't need you.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:46.320
You'll be paid. You can go.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.950
But the accident today-

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:53.830
Unlike our late president,
I'm not superstitious.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.830
You're Subaru Sumeragi,
aren't you?

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:00.300
Today's accident was unfortunate...

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:05.930
but it removed an old man who
trusted primitive superstitions.

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:11.450
The accident won't really
affect this project.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:15.450
On the contrary, it may inspire
some of us to work even harder.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:24.630
In the past few years,
we've had several fatal accidents.

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:33.000
Each one has killed an executive
involved in the same project.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:53.450
Coney!

00:11:58.990 --> 00:11:59.960
Wait!

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:20.810
This is-

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:26.480
On sowa hamba shuda saraba
taraman wa hamba shudokan.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:32.830
On sowa hamba shuda saraba
taraman wa hamba shudokan.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:37.330
On basara gini wa
rachi wa taya sowaka.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:42.960
On sowa hamba shuda saraba
taraman wa hamba shudokan.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:46.470
On batarei ya sowaka!

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:00.620
Darn it!

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:04.630
This thing makes it so hard
to sneak up on people.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.070
A curse?

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.430
Yes.

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:16.400
At least, that's what
someone was trying for.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:20.840
But it's full of mistakes-.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.510
How's that?

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:26.550
It was probably
copied from a book.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:30.550
I'll bet it was full of mistakes-
That's pretty common-.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:32.680
Then it won't have any affect.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:36.420
It's still a curse.
It'll cause trouble.

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:41.900
It won't find its target, but
it may disturb the local spirits.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:46.160
I don't really
believe in that stuff.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:50.670
But this site has had a huge
number of fatal accidents.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:54.640
And the same man has
survived every single one.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:58.480
Is it possible for someone
to have infallible luck?

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:04.580
I suppose so if the spirits
protected him at birth.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.490
- Can that happen?
- Yes.

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:11.290
He'd be protected from
any accident or misfortune.

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:17.370
Nothing bad could touch him;
it would hit someone else nearby.

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:20.430
Why do you ask?

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.740
I've met someone like that.

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:31.370
Shinji Nagumo. I did a full
background on him for the case.

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:35.750
Ever since childhood,
he's been at the center of disasters-.

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:40.220
His parents and friends
all died in terrible accidents.

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:51.490
But...

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:55.100
he was hardly ever scratched.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:56.370
Mr. Nagumo?

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:03.640
If you'd tampered
with an elevator...

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:08.880
and you knew it would fall,
you wouldn't get on, would you?

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:16.060
What kind of man sabotages an
elevator, then climbs on board?

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:17.990
You can't mean-

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:33.140
I'm afraid murder is a bit
outside my line of expertise.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:37.810
Hi!

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:44.180
Good evening.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:54.430
It's the middle of the night!
Where were you?

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.520
You should have
eaten without me.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:16:02.610
We got groceries. I thought
you would be back sooner.

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:05.240
I didn't know what to cook!

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.470
Seishiro, bring that in here.

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:12.410
Anyway, you always forget to eat
when you're working late.

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:15.310
Sol knew you'd be hungry.

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:19.860
Your sister was very
concerned for you.

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.350
You're sooo right!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:27.860
Why do you always cook over here
in Subaru's apartment?

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:33.100
If I cooked at my place, a
“woman's enemy” might show up!

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:34.670
“Woman's enemy?”

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:36.540
La cucaracha!

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:39.670
Oh, I see.

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:51.780
He was the central pillar
of this organization!

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:56.120
He was our guide through
the treacherous seas of business!

00:16:56.250 --> 00:17:00.930
And now that he's been taken
from us, we've lost our way.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.830
We're left behind,
in silent misery.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:14.240
Our plans are still incomplete,
but our leader shall inspire us!

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:19.820
We must devote ourselves to
completing his final project...

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:22.710
in memory of our president.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:36.000
The chairman is the only one left
who still outranks Nagumo.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.440
What's his name?

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:46.910
Coney.

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:49.940
Coney?

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.710
He's a cute dog.

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.450
Is your leg better?

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.060
How did you-

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:09.960
There.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:11.430
What is that?

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:14.960
It's a ward. An invocation.

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:16.700
An invocation?

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:22.270
For when the curse returns.
Haven't you had nightmares?

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:29.250
Curses always return
to their caster.

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:32.380
Your nightmares are a warning.

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:35.020
How did you know?

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:42.260
We've met before. Back when
I ran into you and that night.

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:44.900
That was you?

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:48.700
I didn't see you clearly,
but I heard Coney barking.

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:53.610
I love dogs. I can identify them
from their bark.

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:58.240
Besides, one of my friends is
a vet at an animal hospital.

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:01.720
So that's why
you were at the vet!

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:05.020
I've been worried
about you ever since.

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:11.360
You looked so sad.
I knew you were really upset.

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:23.040
Do you mind if I take a look?

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:24.970
No, go ahead.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:28.540
I knew it.
This is filled with mistakes.

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:34.550
They even misspelled
the most important word.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:37.520
Aren't you going to ask?

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:40.090
Aren't you curious?

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:43.960
Don't you want to know
why l did it?

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:52.630
Coney was a present
from my brother.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:57.210
He worried about me when he
worked late, so he got a dog.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:00.740
He loved Coney
even more than I did.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:06.010
And Coney adored him.
That was the kind of man he was.

00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:09.050
What kind of work did he do?

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:10.640
He was an architect.

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:14.160
He did all the design
for that building, you know.

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:17.160
- The MCC Corporation-
- Yes.

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:19.590
It was his dream.

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:22.670
He planned it and
started the project.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:25.270
He wanted to build
something magnificent:

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:29.640
An intelligent skyscraper
laced with fiber optics.

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:31.800
I never understood the details.

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:36.570
But when he talked about it,
he was like a child on Christmas.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:37.650
But-

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:40.680
Did he pass away?

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.980
No, he was murdered!

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:50.190
It was a year ago.
He fell off the 17th floor.

00:20:50.820 --> 00:20:53.020
The police said
it was an accident.

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:55.360
Everyone said,
“it was such a shame...

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:59.830
when he was so close to
fulfilling his dream.”

00:20:59.930 --> 00:21:03.810
“We were so sorry to hear
about the tragic accident.”

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:09.350
Six months earlier, his boss had
died in another fatal accident.

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:11.850
The police had arrested Nagumo.

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:15.820
They had to release him
for lack of evidence.

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:19.580
But the management
still suspected Nagumo.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:25.930
They were about to fire him
when my brother intervened.

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:30.630
He argued that Nagumo
was crucial to the project.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:34.600
He convinced the president
to keep Nagumo on.

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:40.000
Then my brother
went to see Nagumo.

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:45.340
He said he wouldn't be home
until late that night.

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:49.620
But he never came home.

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:52.650
Have you told
the police about this?

00:21:55.550 --> 00:21:57.720
They both fell.

00:21:59.390 --> 00:22:00.690
What?

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:05.590
My brother and Nagumo
both fell.

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:11.140
Nagumo miraculously survived.
He was caught in a safety net.

00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:13.270
My brother died.

00:22:13.400 --> 00:22:17.780
It was no miracle! I won't
let Nagumo get away with it!

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:20.110
Kazami!

00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:23.120
Maybe they WERE just accidents!

00:22:24.340 --> 00:22:29.090
Do you think the elevator crash
was an accident too?

00:22:29.180 --> 00:22:34.030
I've seen too many accidents,
and the police can't stop them!

00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:37.430
If Nagumo can kill
and get away with it...

00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:39.230
then so can I.

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:40.800
No!

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:45.810
One of the detectives is trying
very hard to catch Nagumo.

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:47.740
Don't give up on the police.

00:22:47.830 --> 00:22:50.750
How can you be so naive?

00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:52.820
I know one thing for sure;

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:58.290
Everyone in Nagumo's way
has died in an accident.

00:22:59.080 --> 00:23:01.920
Thank you for
correcting my spell.

00:23:02.050 --> 00:23:03.720
I won't make that mistake again.

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:04.790
No, don't!

00:23:05.080 --> 00:23:07.960
You're heading for a catastrophe!

00:23:08.090 --> 00:23:11.070
I don't care!
Come on, Coney.

00:23:11.190 --> 00:23:13.930
Your brother wouldn't
have wanted this!

00:23:14.060 --> 00:23:15.870
Kazami!

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:26.510
But the police can't do anything.

00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:31.180
They're helpless without proof.
Suspicion isn't good enough.

00:23:31.310 --> 00:23:35.420
Are you really afraid
she'll try to take revenge?

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:41.000
It's more than that.
She's going up against Nagumo.

00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:43.690
He gives me a strange feeling.

00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:46.000
- Strange?
- Yes.

00:23:46.130 --> 00:23:49.440
I can't quite put
my finger on it.

00:23:49.560 --> 00:23:54.010
I think using magic against him
might rebound disastrously.

00:23:54.130 --> 00:23:56.010
Rebound?

00:23:56.140 --> 00:24:00.550
I think he has some sort of
incredible spiritual power.

00:24:00.670 --> 00:24:02.710
I don't really understand it.

00:24:02.840 --> 00:24:04.790
If you're right,
it could be catastrophic.

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:10.230
Nagumo's power would counter
the force of the girl's hatred.

00:24:10.350 --> 00:24:14.660
The resulting psychic hemorrhage
would be impossible to foresee.

00:24:14.790 --> 00:24:19.600
Setting that much energy loose
would be a disaster.

00:24:20.030 --> 00:24:24.240
Seishiro, when did you
learn about all this stuff?

00:24:25.130 --> 00:24:27.440
You couldn't be-

00:24:27.570 --> 00:24:33.310
Hokuto, you're out of tea!
Here, I'll get you some.

00:24:34.940 --> 00:24:39.150
You're so mean! Why won't you
answer my question?

00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:45.160
You know, maybe you should
think about going on a diet.

00:24:51.290 --> 00:24:56.070
Oh, no! No one will
want to marry me!

00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:45.170
The report gives
the cause of death as shock.

00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:47.810
The president had a weak heart.

00:26:47.940 --> 00:26:53.190
The elevator failure was caused
by metal fatigue in the winch.

00:26:53.450 --> 00:26:59.160
Since it's been declared
an accident, the case is closed.

00:27:00.950 --> 00:27:04.700
Subaru, I was reassigned today.

00:27:04.790 --> 00:27:07.830
I'm being moved to a graft case.

00:27:08.790 --> 00:27:12.440
I was told that this case
is now off limits to me.

00:27:12.530 --> 00:27:16.270
Once Kazami finds out,
she'll be even more depressed.

00:27:16.370 --> 00:27:18.080
Kazami?

00:27:23.110 --> 00:27:24.820
Thanks, mister!

00:27:25.340 --> 00:27:29.850
The MCC Corporation scheduled
an emergency board meeting.

00:27:29.980 --> 00:27:33.660
They want this project to use
the very latest technology.

00:27:33.790 --> 00:27:38.760
But the president is dead and
the CEO is still hospitalized.

00:27:38.890 --> 00:27:42.360
So there's no one left
in Nagumo's way now.

00:27:42.730 --> 00:27:46.610
This project will be the test
for their new president.

00:27:46.730 --> 00:27:49.840
President Shinji Nagumo.

00:27:50.800 --> 00:27:54.750
- Hey, mister!
- Sorry, here you go.

00:28:09.390 --> 00:28:13.800
Well done. We've lost too many
important men since Aso died.

00:28:13.930 --> 00:28:16.770
I was afraid
the company would collapse.

00:28:16.900 --> 00:28:22.210
We gambled everything on
this project, but it's finally done.

00:28:22.330 --> 00:28:26.210
You deserve a good portion
of the credit for that.

00:28:26.910 --> 00:28:29.080
I'm honored.

00:28:33.780 --> 00:28:39.490
You and Aso were to be the
next leaders of this company.

00:28:39.620 --> 00:28:41.930
If only Aso had lived.

00:28:52.860 --> 00:28:55.310
So, will the chairman be next?

00:28:56.370 --> 00:29:01.110
Have you stooped to insults
now that you're off the case?

00:29:02.640 --> 00:29:07.110
If I planned a crime, I certainly
wouldn't leave any evidence.

00:29:07.250 --> 00:29:09.020
I'm sure of that.

00:29:09.150 --> 00:29:11.720
Then you'd better hurry up.

00:29:12.380 --> 00:29:15.460
This project will be officially
finished in two days.

00:29:16.260 --> 00:29:21.930
After that, you'll have to dig
through someone else's garbage.

00:29:33.940 --> 00:29:36.110
Forgive me, Coney!

00:29:39.850 --> 00:29:42.020
Forgive me!

00:30:09.710 --> 00:30:13.250
Just give me an opening, Nagumo.
The game has just begun!

00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:18.490
Hey'.!

00:30:19.150 --> 00:30:20.890
What's wrong?

00:30:23.060 --> 00:30:27.700
Miss Aso! Miss Aso!

00:30:33.470 --> 00:30:35.840
There was a lot of blood on her.

00:30:41.070 --> 00:30:42.250
What did they say?

00:30:42.370 --> 00:30:46.650
The doctors don't know
what's wrong with her.

00:30:48.750 --> 00:30:51.390
- Coney!
- Coney?

00:30:52.720 --> 00:30:54.030
Forgive me.

00:30:54.750 --> 00:30:56.060
Coney!

00:30:58.090 --> 00:31:00.090
A dog-spirit!

00:31:05.100 --> 00:31:07.270
What would Goro Aso's
sister be doing here?

00:31:52.440 --> 00:31:55.080
Hokuto, take care of Kazami.

00:32:30.450 --> 00:32:32.620
Nagumo!

00:32:36.050 --> 00:32:38.230
We're so close!

00:32:39.020 --> 00:32:41.200
Here we go!

00:32:54.670 --> 00:32:57.980
My arm!

00:33:03.450 --> 00:33:04.550
Nagumo!

00:33:13.390 --> 00:33:14.960
Be careful.

00:33:31.580 --> 00:33:34.320
Yamakawa, it's me!

00:33:35.010 --> 00:33:37.460
Yamakawa, where are you?

00:33:56.170 --> 00:33:57.370
Coney-

00:34:00.410 --> 00:34:01.380
Subaru!

00:34:04.510 --> 00:34:05.890
Why did you do this?

00:34:06.380 --> 00:34:08.550
He was unlucky.

00:34:08.650 --> 00:34:11.860
Or maybe I should say
he was lucky.

00:34:12.450 --> 00:34:15.800
Lucky to be present
at my awakening.

00:34:16.090 --> 00:34:17.660
You're controlling
the dog-spirit!

00:34:17.760 --> 00:34:20.000
Do you understand?

00:34:20.130 --> 00:34:23.660
Do you know how much power
is flowing through me?

00:34:23.900 --> 00:34:26.540
I've become more than human!

00:34:27.400 --> 00:34:28.470
It's coming!

00:34:38.080 --> 00:34:39.450
“Demon bane”

00:34:50.260 --> 00:34:52.260
Subaru!

00:35:20.250 --> 00:35:23.320
Show me your power,
Subaru Sumeragi!

00:36:58.420 --> 00:37:01.760
The dog-spirit will
not return to you.

00:37:12.230 --> 00:37:13.900
I had to win.

00:37:14.030 --> 00:37:17.740
I had to beat Aso,
no matter what.

00:37:18.140 --> 00:37:21.780
That's why I jumped off.
And I won my bet.

00:37:22.640 --> 00:37:26.450
I won. There must
be some mistake here!

00:37:26.580 --> 00:37:28.750
This city chose me.

00:37:29.580 --> 00:37:30.820
Nagumo.

00:37:31.320 --> 00:37:34.760
That's right! When Aso died,
the city chose ME!

00:37:34.890 --> 00:37:36.870
The city...

00:37:36.990 --> 00:37:39.160
needs me!

00:37:52.340 --> 00:37:53.980
ME!

00:37:54.810 --> 00:37:57.410
Yes, I have been chosen!

00:38:00.680 --> 00:38:02.850
The City!

00:38:11.460 --> 00:38:15.030
Your desires and
the needs of this city...

00:38:15.790 --> 00:38:19.070
are completely
inconsequential to me.

00:38:23.840 --> 00:38:26.650
But I will not allow you
to harm Subaru.

00:38:33.380 --> 00:38:35.820
I think you'll find that...

00:38:36.650 --> 00:38:39.690
I'm not as gentle as Subaru.

00:39:54.730 --> 00:39:57.100
It's over.

00:39:57.430 --> 00:39:59.970
Don't scare me like that,
Subaru.

00:40:03.230 --> 00:40:04.800
Who are you?

00:40:04.940 --> 00:40:07.110
Subaru's sister.

00:40:12.310 --> 00:40:13.760
Where's Nagumo?

00:40:13.850 --> 00:40:15.690
It's all over now.

00:40:18.550 --> 00:40:21.690
Your pain will probably
never completely heal...

00:40:21.820 --> 00:40:24.390
but it's time for you
to move on.

00:40:25.060 --> 00:40:27.970
You'll meet someone special
and fall in love.

00:40:28.090 --> 00:40:30.970
You have to let go of the past.

00:40:31.900 --> 00:40:35.810
Let go of your revenge
and learn to be happy.

00:40:36.670 --> 00:40:39.080
For the sake of your brother.

00:41:01.590 --> 00:41:06.800
If you'd let loose, he wouldn't
have given you much trouble.

00:41:06.900 --> 00:41:08.570
The detective-

00:41:08.700 --> 00:41:11.940
Don't worry.
Yamakawa is going to be fine.

00:41:12.700 --> 00:41:15.650
You're always so tender-hearted.

00:41:16.810 --> 00:41:20.350
If you're too soft and
let someone kill you...

00:41:20.480 --> 00:41:22.720
you'll end up
making Hokuto cry.
